cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this code, cite TRELLIS.2, Pixal3D and the org's ggml port they are vendored from.
title: trellis2.cpp / pixal3d-ggml, the org's C++/ggml port of TRELLIS.2 and Pixal3D (vendored)
abstract: >-
  git subtree (squashed) of V-Sekai-fire/pixal3d-ggml at 1c22f5e: a
  single-file C++/ggml implementation of the TRELLIS.2 image-to-3D pipeline
  (trellis2.h / trellis2.cpp, the C ABI trellis2_capi, mesh_export with
  vendored xatlas and meshoptimizer, stb), which the dress-on loop's infer
  stage replaces its FoxGirl infer fixture with (Cut 7). At 1c22f5e the tree
  is TRELLIS.2 only (no Pixal3D code); Pixal3D's projection-attention
  conditioning is the port to come. Local adaptations:
  (1) naf.h / naf.cpp, new files (not upstream): NAF, Pixal3D's DINOv3
  feature upsampler (valeoai/NAF, mirrored as V-Sekai-fire/NAF @37f2dfc,
  Apache-2.0), written as ggml graph code from the op census in
  gates/7-pixal3d/aux-models/naf.md: reflect-padded 3x3 conv as a host
  im2col table + GET_ROWS + MUL_MAT, GroupNorm(8) as NORM + MUL + ADD,
  integer average pooling as RESHAPE + MEAN, 2-D axial RoPE as two NEOX ROPE
  passes (base 1, host freq factors), and natten na2d in its exact block
  form (GET_ROWS over a host window table + MUL_MAT + SOFT_MAX_EXT + MUL_MAT),
  evaluated per block range. Weights from tools/models/convert_naf_to_gguf.py.
  (2) nothing else in the tree yet. The host build (tests/native/infer/CMakeLists.txt)
  lists the library sources against the org ggml (V-Sekai-fire/ggml;
  C:/contract-manifest 2-contract/ggml @04b55bba on the host until Cut 3
  lands vendor/ggml), ggml-cpu only, instead of the upstream
  CMakeLists.txt's bundled or workspace-relative ggml.
  Adaptations to come, recorded here as they land: Pixal3D's
  projection-attention blocks and the Aero-Ex GGUF schema (architecture
  'flux', bf16/f16/f32 mix, comfy.gguf.orig_shape reshapes for ss_flow,
  torch-key tensor names, rope phases recomputed from config); weights
  streamed via host UPLOAD instead of file paths (the guest has no
  filesystem); one thread in the guest; the ggml backend swapped to
  ggml-rd over RenderingDevice.
